<title>USA: NGPL confirms &quot;critical time&quot; on gas line.</title>
<headline>NGPL confirms &quot;critical time&quot; on gas line.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natural Gas Pipeline said Friday that it has declared a &quot;critical time&quot; for Saturday deliveries on its gas pipeline system, limiting shippers to only nominated supplies, due to cold.</p>
<p>&quot;You can only take what you nominate,&quot; a company spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>Most temperatures in the central U.S. have fallen to below-freezing levels, stretching as far south as Houston, Texas, where temperatures have registered 32 degrees Fahrenheit.</p>
<p>NGPL, a unit of Occidental Petroleum, runs from western Texas to Illinois.</p>
<p>((--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
